  "final": "I changed `src/ledger.ts` and `src/service.ts` so retries and repeated calls can't debit twice. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes. I didn't add new checks, so the retry, concurrency and conflict paths haven't been run.\n\n**`Ledger.apply`**\n- It remembers each `(tenant, key)` pair together with its amount and receipt.\n- A repeat with the same amount returns the original receipt and adds no new entry.\n- A repeat with a different amount throws `Error('key conflict')` and adds no debit.\n- The lookup and the write happen in the same synchronous step, with no `await` between them. Two concurrent calls with the same key therefore can't both debit.\n- The map key is `JSON.stringify([tenant, key])`, so tenants can't collide with each other.\n\n**`PaymentService.pay`**\n- It checks all input before touching the ledger or transport. Tenant and key must be non-empty strings, cents a positive integer, and attempts an integer from 1 to 5. Anything else throws `Error('invalid payment')`.\n- It now debits once, then retries only `transport.acknowledge`, passing the same receipt each time. Before, it re-applied the debit on every retry.\n- It retries only `Transient`, up to `attempts` total tries. If the tries run out, the last `Transient` is rethrown. Any other error is thrown immediately without a retry.",
  "tools": [
